19,20c
//   - SHORTS (0x200): COMPARE[n]_CLEAR (bit n) and COMPARE[n]_STOP
//     (bit 16 + n) run CLEAR / STOP when COMPARE[n] fires, as on hardware.
//     The network core's controller sets COMPARE0_CLEAR on TIMER0 and then
//     schedules the radio relative to the cleared count; without the short
//     the count ran on past CC[0] and a later start time looked already
//     passed (controller assert, CF-67).
//
// Not implemented (accesses log UNIMPL): ONESHOTEN[n] (0x580), INTEN (0x300).
.
